From 2d5d141e229376869a205ec81e887e929bdc2d18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:07:55 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] drm/asahi: take only the VM reservation in
 drop_mappings_before()

aurora-wip now takes GpuVm::exec_lock_vm() for every VA update, and
drop_mappings_now() unmaps under the VM reservation alone (f3cc4a691438,
"drm/asahi: lock only the VM reservation for VA updates"). The deferred
close path from omacom 13c3371ce23d was written against the full
exec_lock(), which also locks the reservation of every external object,
and the merge kept that call.

Use exec_lock_vm() there too. The newest-binding check still runs under
the lock every bind takes, and the unmap needs nothing more than the VM
reservation and each object's gpuva lock, as in drop_mappings_now().

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
